  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Employee Feedback Form FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an employee feedback form?\", \"a\": \"An employee feedback form is a form employees use to tell their employer what is working and what is not, whether that is a jammed machine or a draft policy. It stays open year-round instead of running once a year, and each comment lands with someone who can fix the problem.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create an employee feedback form?\", \"a\": \"Decide which topics employees will raise and who owns each one. Then describe the form in plain English to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>, which builds the fields, the routing by topic, and a database for every response. File a few real comments yourself before you share the link.\"}, {\"q\": \"What questions should a staff feedback form ask?\", \"a\": \"Start with three questions: what the note is about, what happened or what you suggest, and whether the person wants a reply. Add a name field and make it optional. Ask for a 1-to-5 rating only when you plan to compare scores later, such as a new tool's score after its first month.\"}, {\"q\": \"How is an employee feedback form different from a customer feedback form?\", \"a\": \"They differ in who answers and who follows up. A general <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/feedback'>feedback form</a> asks customers or visitors about a product or a visit, and replies come from support. An employee feedback form asks staff about their own work. Every topic needs an internal owner, and the form should say who reads it.\"}, {\"q\": \"Who should see the answers on an employee feedback form?\", \"a\": \"Only the people who own a topic, plus whoever runs the form. Send pay questions to payroll alone, and keep a manager out of comments about that manager. With Emergent, every response is saved in a database you own, and you decide who can open each topic.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should happen after someone submits an employee feedback form?\", \"a\": \"The employee should get a confirmation on screen, and the comment should reach its owner the same day. Track each one until it is closed, and email the employee when it changes hands or gets fixed. A weekly list of comments nobody has picked up shows which owners are behind.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is an employee feedback form the same as a performance review?\", \"a\": \"No. A performance review judges one employee's work. Federal rules, for example, define an appraisal as \\\"the process under which performance is reviewed and evaluated.\\\" An employee feedback form runs the other way, with staff reporting on the workplace. To score skills against set criteria, use an <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/assessment'>assessment form</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"How long should an employee feedback form be?\", \"a\": \"Keep it to 3 to 5 questions with one open text box, which takes about 2 minutes on a phone. Save long question sets for an annual survey. Forms built with Emergent have no response caps, and a short form that people use every day never runs into a limit.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can an employee feedback form work on a phone for staff without a desk?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Post a QR code in the break room or at the loading dock, and the form opens in the phone's browser. Make the topic a tap instead of a typed answer to keep typing short. Emergent can build it as a one-question-per-screen flow, which suits a small screen.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should an employee feedback form also ask about staff preferences?\", \"a\": \"Keep preferences on a separate form. Feedback needs an owner and a status, while preferences such as favorite snacks or how someone likes to be thanked are reference notes for a manager. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/favorite-things-questionnaire'>favorite things questionnaire</a> collects those, and the two stay easier to read apart.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
